From 28d06d2bceca23dadb3c8997c770635a2be13d97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:50:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(ui): camcraft-ui builds and links for wasm32 (#31
 rung 2)

Cut the native-only seams out of the shared UI so camcraft-ui.wasm links
for wasm32-unknown-unknown next to rung 1's camcraft-cli.wasm:

- egui_app/shell.rs split: the winit loop, window, surface and GPU
  bring-up move to egui_app/shell_window.rs, the per-frame draw and the
  ApplicationHandler to shell_window/frame.rs. They (plus gpu_init,
  frame_watch, os_quit) are native-only. shell.rs keeps the shared frame
  (shell_layout, dock tabs, viewport panel, headless proof). On wasm32
  egui_app::run refuses the windowed entry by name (exit 2).
- file_dialog: one FileDialog seam for the 13 rfd sites; native forwards
  to rfd unchanged, wasm32 answers None (cancelled) with a diagnostic.
  egui-winit and rfd become native-only dependencies.
- camcraft_app::clock::Instant: std's Instant natively, web_time's on
  wasm32 (std's panics there). web-time 1.1 was already in the lock.
  geometry's projection profiler reads the clock only when profiling.
- web/build-app-wasm.sh also builds and links camcraft-ui.wasm.

The browser runner, async GPU bring-up, async file picker, thread
fallbacks and the wasi JS shim are still owed.

Refs #31

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
