+# then builds and links camcraft-ui.wasm for the same target (rung 2).
 # Provenance: our own build script; the toolchain facts come from the public
 # wasi-sdk release notes and the cc / cargo `--config` documentation.
 #
@@ -98,3 +99,15 @@ cargo build -p camcraft-app --target wasm32-unknown-unknown "${PROFILE_ARGS[@]}"
 OUT="${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-$ROOT/target}/wasm32-unknown-unknown/$([[ ${#PROFILE_ARGS[@]} -gt 0 ]] && echo release || echo debug)/camcraft-cli.wasm"
 [[ -f "$OUT" ]] || die "build reported success but $OUT is missing"
 echo "build-app-wasm: linked $OUT"
+
+# --- 4. rung 2: the UI links for wasm32 -----------------------------------
+# The shared shell (egui_app::shell, file_dialog, the clock seam) builds; the
+# native window (shell_window, egui-winit, rfd) is cfg'd out, so the linked
+# camcraft-ui.wasm refuses the windowed entry by name. The browser runner
+# that will draw the shell is still owed (#31).
+cargo build -p camcraft-ui --bin camcraft-ui --target wasm32-unknown-unknown "${PROFILE_ARGS[@]}" \
+    --config "patch.crates-io.flecs_ecs.path='$(native_path "$PATCHED/flecs_ecs")'" \
+    --config "patch.crates-io.flecs_ecs_sys.path='$(native_path "$PATCHED/flecs_ecs_sys")'"
+UI_OUT="$(dirname "$OUT")/camcraft-ui.wasm"
+[[ -f "$UI_OUT" ]] || die "build reported success but $UI_OUT is missing"
+echo "build-app-wasm: linked $UI_OUT"

From 5eaaa3072e7e68cff24b0a6dabacab9cf49c09b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:49:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(ui): the shell runs in a browser - eframe web
 runner, awaited GPU start-up (#31 rung 3)

The browser shell is egui_app/shell_web.rs (wasm32 only): an eframe::App
over a <canvas> that runs the same shell::shell_layout frame and the same
3D pass as the native window, started from the page through the exported
camcraft_start(canvas_id). eframe awaits the adapter, device and surface;
a refusal is said on the page (#camcraft-status) and in the console,
never a panic.

- view_pass.rs: the scene upload gate, target sizing, View3D + traced
  stock pass and the repaint law, moved unchanged out of the native frame
  so both shells share them.
- The blocking GPU waits get awaited twins: TracePass::new_async,
  Composite::new_async, StockEye::new_async, headless_gpu::device_async.
  The blocking forms are thin native-only wrappers; pollster is now a
  native-only dependency. The native-only trace readback moved to
  trace/readback.rs.
- web/index.html and web/wasi_shim.js: the page, and the nine
  wasi_snapshot_preview1 imports flecs' libc asks for, wired by an
  import map.
- web/build-app-wasm.sh links the UI as a cdylib (cargo rustc
  --crate-type, manifest unchanged), runs the wasm-bindgen CLI pinned by
  Cargo.lock and lays out target/web; it fails if the module asks for a
  WASI import the shim does not answer.

Proved in headless Chrome (WebGL2 through SwiftShader): the module
instantiates, the first frame draws, a click on the ribbon opens the
Stock page. The WebGPU path was not exercised.

Refs #31

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
