From b6483d6698f5534323f111b80de5d464409220ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:40:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(ui): browser diagnostics reach the console; shim
 answers match its comments (#31 review)

Review findings on PR #847:
- crate::diag is the UI crate's one diagnostics seam: diag_warn! and
  diag_info! print to stderr/stdout natively and to the page console on
  wasm32, where std drops both streams. The stock eye's fall-back to the
  CPU march, the file dialog's "cancelled" note and the other direct
  prints in browser-compiled UI code go through it; a law test fails on
  a direct print outside the seam.
- wasi_shim.js: poll_oneoff succeeds at once, reports clock
  subscriptions as elapsed and says the skipped wait in the console
  (it answered ENOSYS under a comment that promised a return). Unknown
  clock ids and closed descriptors answer a named errno with a console
  warning. The functions outside the module's nine imports are removed.
- build-app-wasm.sh: the missing-imports message prints under pipefail;
  the wasm-bindgen install is announced before it runs and
  CAMCRAFT_WASM_NO_INSTALL=1 refuses it with instructions.
- view_pass::target_extent holds the pixel ratio to 0.1..=8 itself, so
  the first browser target is clamped like every later frame.

Refs #31

